config AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND
	bool "Airoha/EcoNet parallel (raw) NAND controller"
	depends on MTD && DM_MTD && ARCH_AIROHA
	help
	  Support for the parallel NAND interface of the Airoha/EcoNet NFI
	  controller, found on the AN7581/AN7583 family.

	  The NFI block drives either a SPI-NAND device (through the SPI
	  controller, see CONFIG_AIROHA_SNFI_SPI) or a parallel NAND bus; the
	  mode is selected by the boot strap and reported by the hardware, so
	  only one of the two drivers claims the block at runtime.

	  Enable this when the board wires a raw NAND device to the NFI and
	  describes it with a "airoha,en7581-nand" device tree node.

config AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND_TIMING
	bool "Program the parallel NAND AC timing register"
	depends on AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND
	default y
	help
	  Program the AC timing register (_PARALLEL_NFI_REGS_ACCCON) instead of
	  keeping the hardware default.

	  Keep this enabled on the AN7581/AN7583: the register default leaves
	  every timing field at its maximum, which limits the interface to about
	  3.9 MiB/s, and the boot stage does not calibrate the register.  The
	  device table carries the legacy 112.5 MHz value for most devices, so
	  entries using it are programmed with the 150 MHz setting instead.

	  Only boards whose boot chain already programs a calibrated value for
	  their APB rate should turn this off.

	  A board whose device needs a different setting can state the raw
	  register value in the device tree, where it takes precedence over the
	  value from the device table:

	      airoha,ac-timing = <0x40044326>;

	  Instead of the raw value an ONFI async SDR timing mode can be asked
	  for, the driver then derives every field and the data sampling strobe
	  from the ONFI timings:

	      airoha,nand-timing-mode = <1>;      /* 0..5 */

	  Individual fields can be overridden on top of either of the two, which
	  is what board tuning needs.  Note that a short RE# low time (small
	  rlt) also needs the strobe, otherwise the data is sampled too early:

	      airoha,ac-timing-rlt = <1>;
	      airoha,ac-timing-wh = <1>;
	      airoha,ac-timing-strobe = <1>;

config AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND_GEOMETRY_SPARE
	bool "Select parallel NAND spare stride from physical OOB geometry"
	depends on AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND && TARGET_AN7581
	help
	  Match the pbs05 AN7581 U-Boot/ponwrt page format: choose the largest
	  supported sector spare size within the physical NAND OOB geometry,
	  independently of BCH strength. ECC4 with 2K pages and 128-byte OOB
	  uses 28 spare bytes per sector instead of the vendor 16-byte stride.
	  This changes the on-flash encoding. Existing vendor-layout UBI data
	  requires backup and coordinated BL23/U-Boot/OS migration. Enable only
	  with the matching ATF geometry-spare patch; do not mix old/new images.

config AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND_READ_ONLY
	bool "Disable parallel NAND programming and erase (RAM diagnostics)"
	depends on AIROHA_PARALLEL_NAND
	help
	  Reject page programming and block erase at the driver primitives,
	  including OOB writes and bad-block marking. Intended for RAM-loaded
	  diagnostics, not installation or recovery writes.
